TOPIC

about_IISWebFarmClasses

SHORT DESCRIPTION

Describes the classes implemented by IISWebFarm.

LONG DESCRIPTION

IISWebFarm uses strongly typed PowerShell classes
to provide predictable and structured output.

Classes provide a stable contract between:

* Validation functions
* Logging
* JSON serialization
* Reporting
* Notifications
* Future integrations

IMPLEMENTED CLASSES

BaseResult

Base class for module result objects.

Provides common functionality shared by all result
types.

The BaseResult class is intended to act as the
foundation for future result classes.

FUTURE CLASSES

The following classes are planned or partially
designed:

IISWebFarmSettings

Represents validated module configuration.

IISWebFarmMailSettings

Represents validated mail configuration.

IISWebFarmExecutionContext

Represents execution metadata including:

* RunId
* Version
* Start time
* End time
* User context

IISWebFarmLogContext

Represents logging configuration and log paths.

IISWebFarmValidationResult

Represents validation output generated by
verification functions.

IISWebFarmResult

Represents a complete Verify-WebFarm execution.

CLASS DESIGN RULES

Classes should:

* Have a single responsibility
* Support structured serialization
* Avoid presentation logic
* Prefer explicit property names
* Remain backwards compatible

New result types should derive from BaseResult
whenever practical.

SERIALIZATION

Classes should be serializable to:

* Hashtable
* JSON
* JSONL

Future integrations may consume serialized
objects directly.

